  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "1.1.0-beta\n\t\t\tAdds HasEverRequestedAuthority(...) to distinguish epoch participation history\n\t\t\tfrom currently held authority. This affects only custom IAuthorityEpochProvider\n\t\t\timplementations. The provided concrete implementation supports this\n\t\t\tautomatically and serves as a guide to add equivalent epoch-history tracking.\n\n\t\t\t1.0.3\n\t\t\tAdds TestableEpoch support for deterministic Guid and DateTimeOffset\n\t\t\tgeneration in unit tests, along with documentation and broader MSTest\n\t\t\tcoverage for repeatable fixture generation.\n\n\t\t\t1.0.2\n\t\t\tImproves usability by adding the default\n\t\t\tCancelAuthorityEpoch(@throw = false) behavior and promoting generic\n\t\t\tAuthority and Authorities members for easier direct consumption.\n\n\t\t\t1.0.1\n\t\t\tStrengthens the generic API with runtime type enforcement and expanded\n\t\t\ttest coverage for cancellation, mixed-authority scenarios, lifecycle\n\t\t\tinvariants, awaitable completion, and context snapshot behavior.\n\n\t\t\t1.0.0\n\t\t\tInitial release of AuthorityEpochProvider for authority-based coordination\n\t\t\tover DisposableHost epochs, including first-wins authority selection,\n\t\t\treference-counted participation, and deterministic FinalDispose behavior.",
